      * In-program suite on LOANBTCH: the cases run inside a copy of the
      * batch, with the master file, the transactions, the rejects, the
      * clock and the call to LOANCALC mocked case by case. Two kinds of
      * case live side by side on the same program:
      *  - interface: the master file and the date go in, and only what
      *    comes out through the files is checked (the first case). They
      *    stay valid after a rewrite, even if the language changes.
      *  - internal: they run a single paragraph and look at the
      *    WORKING-STORAGE. They locate defects while the COBOL lives.
      * It includes a case that fails because of a defect seeded in the
      * program (see the header comment of src/LOANBTCH.cbl).
       TESTSUITE TSTBATCH 'Loan settlement (in-program)'
       PROGRAM LOANBTCH

       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01  WS-LAST-DEBIT             PIC X(60).
       01  WS-LAST-REJECT            PIC X(60).
       01  WS-DEBIT-WRITES           PIC 9(3).
       01  WS-DEBIT-LINES.
           05  WS-DEBIT-CAP          PIC X(60) OCCURS 10 TIMES.

       BEFORE-EACH
           MOVE ZERO TO WS-READ-COUNT WS-DEBIT-COUNT WS-REJECT-COUNT
                        WS-SKIP-COUNT WS-LINE-COUNT WS-TOTAL-DEBIT
                        WS-DEBIT-WRITES
           MOVE SPACES TO WS-LAST-DEBIT WS-LAST-REJECT WS-DEBIT-LINES
           MOVE "N" TO WS-EOF
      * master file with two active loans; each case may redefine it
           MOCK FILE LOAN-FILE
               ON READ
                   EVALUATE CBLT-READ-COUNT
                       WHEN 1
                           MOVE "PR000001" TO LOAN-ID
                           MOVE "GARCIA" TO LOAN-CUSTOMER
                           MOVE 100000 TO LOAN-PRINCIPAL
                           MOVE 0.36 TO LOAN-ANNUAL-RATE
                           MOVE 12 TO LOAN-TERM-MONTHS
                           MOVE 20260131 TO LOAN-START-DATE
                           MOVE "A" TO LOAN-STATUS
                       WHEN 2
                           MOVE "PR000002" TO LOAN-ID
                           MOVE "LOPEZ" TO LOAN-CUSTOMER
                           MOVE 250000 TO LOAN-PRINCIPAL
                           MOVE 0.24 TO LOAN-ANNUAL-RATE
                           MOVE 36 TO LOAN-TERM-MONTHS
                           MOVE 20260215 TO LOAN-START-DATE
                           MOVE "A" TO LOAN-STATUS
                       WHEN OTHER
                           SET CBLT-AT-END TO TRUE
                   END-EVALUATE
           END-MOCK
           MOCK FILE DEBIT-FILE
               ON WRITE
                   ADD 1 TO WS-DEBIT-WRITES
                   MOVE DEBIT-REC TO WS-LAST-DEBIT
                   IF WS-DEBIT-WRITES <= 10
                       MOVE DEBIT-REC TO WS-DEBIT-CAP(WS-DEBIT-WRITES)
                   END-IF
           END-MOCK
           MOCK FILE REJECT-FILE
               ON WRITE
                   MOVE REJECT-REC TO WS-LAST-REJECT
           END-MOCK
       END-BEFORE

       TESTCASE 'interface: master file goes in, transactions come out'
      * Interface case: only the mocked master file and the date go in
      * and only the output files are checked. RUN executes the whole
      * original flow; its STOP RUN ends the case, not the process.
           MOCK CLOCK
               DATE '260301'
           END-MOCK
           RUN
           VERIFY STOP HAPPENED ONCE
           EXPECT WS-DEBIT-WRITES TO BE NUMERIC 4
           EXPECT WS-DEBIT-CAP(1) TO BE 'SETTLEMENT  20260301'
           EXPECT WS-DEBIT-CAP(2) TO CONTAIN 'PR000001 GARCIA'
           EXPECT WS-DEBIT-CAP(2) TO CONTAIN '10046.21 20260228 INSTALLMENT'
           EXPECT WS-DEBIT-CAP(3) TO CONTAIN 'PR000002 LOPEZ'
           EXPECT WS-DEBIT-CAP(3) TO CONTAIN '9808.21 20260315'
           EXPECT WS-DEBIT-CAP(4) TO CONTAIN 'CONTROL'
           EXPECT WS-DEBIT-CAP(4) TO CONTAIN '19854.42'
           EXPECT WS-LAST-REJECT TO BE SPACES
           VERIFY CALL 'LOANCALC' HAPPENED 2 TIMES
           VERIFY WRITE DEBIT-FILE HAPPENED 4 TIMES
           VERIFY WRITE REJECT-FILE NEVER HAPPENED
           VERIFY CLOSE LOAN-FILE HAPPENED ONCE

      * The cases that follow are internal: they run a single paragraph
      * and look at WORKING-STORAGE fields.
       TESTCASE 'two active loans with the real LOANCALC'
           PERFORM 2000-PROCESS
           EXPECT WS-READ-COUNT TO BE NUMERIC 2
           EXPECT WS-DEBIT-COUNT TO BE NUMERIC 2
           EXPECT WS-REJECT-COUNT TO BE ZEROS
      * 10046.21 (GARCIA) + 9808.21 (LOPEZ)
           EXPECT WS-TOTAL-DEBIT TO BE NUMERIC 19854.42
           EXPECT WS-LAST-DEBIT TO CONTAIN 'LOPEZ'
           EXPECT WS-LAST-DEBIT TO CONTAIN '9808.21 20260315'
           VERIFY CALL 'LOANCALC' HAPPENED 2 TIMES
           VERIFY READ LOAN-FILE HAPPENED 3 TIMES
           VERIFY WRITE DEBIT-FILE HAPPENED 2 TIMES
           VERIFY WRITE REJECT-FILE NEVER HAPPENED
           VERIFY PARAGRAPH 3000-END NEVER HAPPENED

       TESTCASE 'mocked installment: the batch without the calculation'
           MOCK CALL 'LOANCALC'
               MOVE 1000 TO WS-L-INSTALLMENT
               MOVE 20260301 TO WS-L-FIRST-DUE
               MOVE "00" TO WS-L-RETURN-CODE
           END-MOCK
           PERFORM 2000-PROCESS
           EXPECT WS-TOTAL-DEBIT TO BE NUMERIC 2000
           EXPECT WS-LAST-DEBIT TO CONTAIN '1000.00 20260301'
           VERIFY CALL 'LOANCALC' HAPPENED 2 TIMES
           VERIFY PARAGRAPH 2200-WRITE-DEBIT HAPPENED 2 TIMES

       TESTCASE 'LOANCALC rejects: the loan goes to rejects'
           MOCK CALL 'LOANCALC'
               EXPECT WS-L-PRINCIPAL TO BE GREATER THAN ZERO
               MOVE "40" TO WS-L-RETURN-CODE
           END-MOCK
           PERFORM 2000-PROCESS
           EXPECT WS-DEBIT-COUNT TO BE ZEROS
           EXPECT WS-REJECT-COUNT TO BE NUMERIC 2
           EXPECT WS-TOTAL-DEBIT TO BE ZEROS
           EXPECT WS-LAST-REJECT TO CONTAIN 'PR000002 40'
           EXPECT WS-LAST-REJECT TO CONTAIN 'INVALID START DATE'
           VERIFY WRITE REJECT-FILE HAPPENED 2 TIMES
           VERIFY WRITE DEBIT-FILE NEVER HAPPENED

      * The four reject reasons, with the real LOANCALC: each one goes
      * through its WHEN in the EVALUATE of 2300-WRITE-REJECT.
       TESTCASE 'reject 10: zero principal'
           MOCK FILE LOAN-FILE
               ON READ
                   IF CBLT-READ-COUNT = 1
                       MOVE "PR000010" TO LOAN-ID
                       MOVE "RUIZ" TO LOAN-CUSTOMER
                       MOVE 0 TO LOAN-PRINCIPAL
                       MOVE 0.36 TO LOAN-ANNUAL-RATE
                       MOVE 12 TO LOAN-TERM-MONTHS
                       MOVE 20260131 TO LOAN-START-DATE
                       MOVE "A" TO LOAN-STATUS
                   ELSE
                       SET CBLT-AT-END TO TRUE
                   END-IF
           END-MOCK
           PERFORM 2000-PROCESS
           EXPECT WS-REJECT-COUNT TO BE NUMERIC 1
           EXPECT WS-DEBIT-COUNT TO BE ZEROS
           EXPECT WS-LAST-REJECT TO BE 'PR000010 10 ZERO PRINCIPAL'
           VERIFY CALL 'LOANCALC' HAPPENED ONCE

       TESTCASE 'reject 20: term out of range'
           MOCK FILE LOAN-FILE
               ON READ
                   IF CBLT-READ-COUNT = 1
                       MOVE "PR000020" TO LOAN-ID
                       MOVE "RUIZ" TO LOAN-CUSTOMER
                       MOVE 100000 TO LOAN-PRINCIPAL
                       MOVE 0.36 TO LOAN-ANNUAL-RATE
                       MOVE 400 TO LOAN-TERM-MONTHS
                       MOVE 20260131 TO LOAN-START-DATE
                       MOVE "A" TO LOAN-STATUS
                   ELSE
                       SET CBLT-AT-END TO TRUE
                   END-IF
           END-MOCK
           PERFORM 2000-PROCESS
           EXPECT WS-REJECT-COUNT TO BE NUMERIC 1
           EXPECT WS-LAST-REJECT TO BE 'PR000020 20 TERM OUT OF RANGE'

       TESTCASE 'reject 30: rate out of range'
           MOCK FILE LOAN-FILE
               ON READ
                   IF CBLT-READ-COUNT = 1
                       MOVE "PR000030" TO LOAN-ID
                       MOVE "RUIZ" TO LOAN-CUSTOMER
                       MOVE 100000 TO LOAN-PRINCIPAL
                       MOVE 2.5 TO LOAN-ANNUAL-RATE
                       MOVE 12 TO LOAN-TERM-MONTHS
                       MOVE 20260131 TO LOAN-START-DATE
                       MOVE "A" TO LOAN-STATUS
                   ELSE
                       SET CBLT-AT-END TO TRUE
                   END-IF
           END-MOCK
           PERFORM 2000-PROCESS
           EXPECT WS-REJECT-COUNT TO BE NUMERIC 1
           EXPECT WS-LAST-REJECT TO BE 'PR000030 30 RATE OUT OF RANGE'

       TESTCASE 'an unknown return code goes to rejects as uncataloged'
      * LOANCALC does not return "99" today; the batch has to survive a
      * new code anyway, so the call is mocked
           MOCK CALL 'LOANCALC'
               MOVE "99" TO WS-L-RETURN-CODE
           END-MOCK
           PERFORM 2000-PROCESS
           EXPECT WS-REJECT-COUNT TO BE NUMERIC 2
           EXPECT WS-LAST-REJECT TO BE 'PR000002 99 UNCATALOGED ERROR'

       TESTCASE 'a closed loan is neither settled nor calculated'
           MOCK FILE LOAN-FILE
               ON READ
                   IF CBLT-READ-COUNT = 1
                       MOVE "PR000009" TO LOAN-ID
                       MOVE "PEREZ" TO LOAN-CUSTOMER
                       MOVE 5000 TO LOAN-PRINCIPAL
                       MOVE "C" TO LOAN-STATUS
                   ELSE
                       SET CBLT-AT-END TO TRUE
                   END-IF
           END-MOCK
           PERFORM 2000-PROCESS
           EXPECT WS-SKIP-COUNT TO BE NUMERIC 1
           EXPECT WS-DEBIT-COUNT TO BE ZEROS
           EXPECT WS-LAST-DEBIT TO BE SPACES
           VERIFY CALL 'LOANCALC' NEVER HAPPENED

       TESTCASE 'empty master file: no transactions and no calls'
           MOCK FILE LOAN-FILE
               ON READ AT END
           END-MOCK
           PERFORM 2000-PROCESS
           EXPECT WS-END-OF-FILE TO BE TRUE
           EXPECT WS-READ-COUNT TO BE ZEROS
           VERIFY READ LOAN-FILE HAPPENED ONCE
           VERIFY CALL 'LOANCALC' NEVER HAPPENED

       TESTCASE 'the header carries the process date with century'
           MOCK CLOCK
               DATE '260301'
           END-MOCK
           PERFORM 1000-INIT
           EXPECT WS-PROCESS-DATE TO BE NUMERIC 260301
           EXPECT WS-LAST-DEBIT TO CONTAIN 'SETTLEMENT  20260301'
           EXPECT WS-DEBIT-STATUS TO BE '00'
           VERIFY OPEN LOAN-FILE HAPPENED ONCE
           VERIFY CLOCK HAPPENED ONCE

       TESTCASE 'the control record counts only the transactions'
      * Fails on purpose: the program reports WS-LINE-COUNT, which
      * includes the header (seeded defect, see src/LOANBTCH.cbl).
      * Expected 2, actual 3: this is what a failure looks like.
           MOCK CLOCK
               DATE '260301'
           END-MOCK
           MOCK CALL 'LOANCALC'
               MOVE 1000 TO WS-L-INSTALLMENT
               MOVE 20260401 TO WS-L-FIRST-DUE
               MOVE "00" TO WS-L-RETURN-CODE
           END-MOCK
           PERFORM 1000-INIT
           PERFORM 2000-PROCESS
           PERFORM 3000-END
           EXPECT WS-DEBIT-WRITES TO BE NUMERIC 4
           EXPECT WS-LAST-DEBIT TO CONTAIN 'CONTROL'
           EXPECT WS-LAST-DEBIT TO CONTAIN '2000.00'
           EXPECT WS-T-COUNT TO BE NUMERIC 2
           VERIFY CLOSE DEBIT-FILE HAPPENED ONCE

       IGNORE
       TESTCASE 'pending: same-day rerun (no rule yet)'
           PERFORM 2000-PROCESS
           EXPECT WS-DEBIT-COUNT TO BE ZEROS
